# Time-dependent reference run for the Bmad FEL tracker: the Benchmark1-SASE
# configuration of Aramis-ss.in with a time window, exercising slippage. Differences from
# Aramis-ss.in, each with its reason:
#
#   - &time with slen = 9.6e-9 and sample = 3. Genesis sets nslice =
#     round(slen/(sample*lambda0)) (GenTime.cpp:70), so this is exactly 32 slices of
#     spacing 3*lambda0. sample = 3 matches the slice spacing to the slippage of one
#     delz = 0.045 m = 3-period step (one slice per step at resonance), the matched
#     configuration of the coarse-step sweep, and the 32-slice window keeps the
#     benchmark's runtime in check -- slippage physics does not depend on window length.
#
#   - shotnoise = 1. In steady state shot noise was disabled to make the run
#     deterministic; here the slice-to-slice variation it creates is the signal that
#     makes slippage observable (with identical quiet slices, every slice would evolve
#     identically and a rotation bug would be invisible). Both codes start from the
#     written dumps, so the realization is shared and determinism is preserved.
#
#   - npart = 2048 (default 8192). The comparison tracks identical particles in both
#     codes, so statistical convergence is not at stake, and 32 slices multiply the work.
#
# Everything else is unchanged: same lattice, same gamma0, same seed field, FFT field
# solver, no harmonics.

&setup
rootname=AramisTD
lattice=Aramis.lat
beamline=ARAMIS
lambda0=1e-10
gamma0=11357.82
delz=0.045000
shotnoise=1
npart = 2048
nbins = 8
beam_global_stat = true
field_global_stat = true
&end

&lattice
zmatch=9.5
&end

&time
slen = 9.6e-9
sample = 3
&end

&field
power=5e3
dgrid=2.000000e-04
ngrid=255
waist_size=30e-6
&end

&beam
current=3000
delgam=1.000000
ex=4.000000e-07
ey=4.000000e-07
&end

&write
field = AramisTD-initial
beam = AramisTD-initial
&end

&track
fft_fieldsolver = true
&end

&write
field = AramisTD-final
beam = AramisTD-final
&end
